+From: Sanjay Ravindran <mail2snjyrvndrn@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: aquantia: add async FW watchdog reload and fix LED blink stretch
+
+Flashless Aquantia AQR114C PHYs run volatile firmware loaded over MDIO
+(e.g., marvell/AQR114C.cld). Cable hotplug transients or internal resets
+can drop the PHY back to boot-ROM (VEND1_GLOBAL_FW_ID 30:0x0020 == 0,
+VEND1_GLOBAL_SC == 0x8000) or stall the firmware heartbeat counter
+(30:0xc886), leaving the 5GbE link permanently down until reboot.
+
+Additionally, VEND1_GLOBAL_LED_PROV_ACT_STRETCH was inverted as
+GENMASK(0, 1) and never enabled in aqr_phy_led_hw_control_set(), leaving
+activity blink stretch at 0 ms so LEDs appear solid on multi-gig links;
+any firmware reset also clears LED provisioning registers (30:0xc430..c43a).
+
+Fix both issues safely without lock stalls, phylib error latches, or
+CPU/MDIO overload:
+- Fix VEND1_GLOBAL_LED_PROV_ACT_STRETCH to GENMASK(1, 0) and enable 100 ms
+  stretch (0x3) when TX/RX netdev hardware offload triggers are requested.
+- Cache and restore PHY LED hardware-control rules alongside polarity in
+  aqr_phy_led_restore() across config_init, resume, and firmware reload.
+- Offload aqr_firmware_reload() (30:0x2680 trigger + NVMEM/FS load +
+  USXGMII C37 AN / LED restore) to an asynchronous work_struct
+  (fw_reload_work on system_unbound_wq), holding neither rtnl_lock nor
+  phydev->lock during the ~29s MDIO upload, and guard concurrent hwmon,
+  ethtool, LED, IRQ, and polling MDIO accesses with fw_reloading.
+- Check MDIO return codes and insert cond_resched() + fw_reload_abort
+  checks every 256 words in aqr_fw_load_memory() for RCU/scheduler health
+  under CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE and rapid cancellation in suspend/remove.
+- Never return reload errors from aqr107_read_status() (avoids permanent
+  PHY_ERROR/PHY_HALTED latch in phylib), apply exponential backoff
+  (30s..300s), and cap consecutive reloads at AQR_FW_RELOAD_MAX_FAILS (5)
+  unless sustained healthy operation (>= 60s) or interface restart occurs.
+
+diff -uNr a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia.h b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia.h
+--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia.h	2026-11-20 17:35:19.263567847 +0000
++++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia.h	2026-11-20 17:39:17.181751400 +0000
